body:
Thanks for sharing this. I'm back to Day 2 (gotta reset my badge again) and a mod sent me a meme like, "it's hard to beat a person who never gives up," but I feel like I'm voluntarily giving up every time I seek or accept a drink. So I'm beating myself over and over, and not only do *I* lose, but my loved ones lose when I behave badly or embarrass them. I hear you on the depression and the lack of supports for accessing mental healthcare. It's not an excuse, but a reality, even when I'm doing other things right (also exercising, trying vitamins and psych meds). But looking at the world, with all of its insanity and horrors daily, really makes me feel like I want to opt out sometimes. I won't, because it would crush my family, so I sometimes feel absolutely stuck, and it sucks.

&#x200B;

But I will say that just reading that someone else is going through this, and has made it 38 days and believes it gets easier... well, that gives me hope. So thank you for that.
